{
 "_doc": "The numbers of comms, transport and boarding (src/Core/Data/SystemsDef.Comms.cs reads them), from the battle console mockup (docs/mockups/battle-console.html: the hail, TRANSPORT, BOARD, INV, TEAM_DEFAULT, each class's pads, hold_t, marines and team, BEAM_FX and STREAM). The Krai and Ssarith Hunt classes take the mockup's numbers for the class of their size (krai_cv the frigate's, krai_ff the destroyer's, krai_ca and krai_dn the heavy cruiser's, the Hunt frigates the Hunt stalker's, hunt_ca and hunt_cv the heavy cruiser's) until their own are set.",
 "hail": {
  "_doc": "What a hailed ship answers (owner, 2026-11-06: \"I should be able to hail other ships, although most enemies wont respond\"): an enemy answers only if its faction has a reply here; the rest say no_answer. A friendly ship answers friend_reply, or friend_needs while it still asks for something ({needs}), or pilot_needed for a prize with no pilot. {name} is the ship's name.",
  "no_answer": "No answer on any channel.",
  "enemy_reply": {
   "krai": "The Warhost does not parley with the weak.",
   "kethran": "The Hegemony does not parley with the weak.",
   "vos": "Your cargo or your hull. Choose quickly."
  },
  "friend_reply": "{name} here. Standing by.",
  "friend_needs": "{name} here. We still need {needs}.",
  "pilot_needed": "{name}: ours, but dead in space. Pilot needed."
 },
 "transport": {
  "_doc": "The transporter's reach (owner, 2026-11-03: \"transport range is too wide! 1.5 km only!\"), shared by boarding, raids and the inventory transporter; the pads (owner, 2026-11-02: one pad beams one person or one load, then recharges, pad_charge_s at one energy point when it charges alone, that times the number charging at once); the longest boarding queue; a shield facing at or under shield_down_hp is down.",
  "range_km": 15,
  "pads_default": 2,
  "pad_charge_s": 8,
  "queue_max": 30,
  "shield_down_hp": 0.5
 },
 "boarding": {
  "_doc": "Boarding (after the-federation's boarding.gd and the owner's survey answers B14 and B15). Hit and run: a squad goes to one subsystem for raid_s; shooting takes shoot_per_marine a combat marine standing (at most shoot_max), bombing bomb_dmg if a demolition marine lives; a demolition marine is lost at demo_loss over (1 + escorting marines), a combat marine at marine_loss. Capture: a volley every volley_s, each marine one shot at hit_chance, both sides at once, the defenders its marines and guard_crew armed crew; a hit wounds a marine by wound; each medic heals the most wounded by heal a volley; each hacker locks out a guard at hacker_lock and shortens the volley by hacker_speed (hacker_speed_max at most), and with fewer than hacker_cover marines a hit finds a hacker at hacker_exposed_p; the envoy talks one defender down at vip_persuade. Taking it needs an engineer and a hacker (or the envoy); a pilot is needed to get it under way.",
  "raid_s": 6,
  "shoot_per_marine": 0.2,
  "shoot_max": 0.6,
  "bomb_dmg": 0.8,
  "demo_loss": 0.6,
  "marine_loss": 0.2,
  "volley_s": 10,
  "hit_chance": 0.5,
  "guard_crew": 2,
  "hacker_lock": 0.5,
  "vip_persuade": 0.5,
  "wound": 0.5,
  "heal": 0.35,
  "hacker_speed": 0.15,
  "hacker_speed_max": 0.5,
  "hacker_cover": 5,
  "hacker_exposed_p": 0.5
 },
 "inventory": {
  "_doc": "The inventory transporter: goods, supplies or the envoy to or from a friendly ship, station or planet in reach; one beam moves per_beam units and spends a pad. A class with no hold of its own has hold_default_t.",
  "per_beam": 5,
  "hold_default_t": 10
 },
